#!/bin/bash
# SessionStart hook. Plain stdout from a SessionStart command hook becomes context for Claude.
# Prompt-type hooks are not supported on SessionStart, so this replaces the old prompt hook.
cat > /dev/null
cat <<'EOF'
The PayIt2 plugin is installed. If PayIt2 tools such as list_my_campaigns are available in this session, the organizer is signed in to PayIt2. In that case, call list_my_campaigns once to find their active campaigns, and call get_campaign_health for any campaign past half its timeline or below 30% of its goal or capacity. Open your first reply with a short greeting of three to five lines that names any urgent campaign and its top recommendation. If they have no campaigns, greet them and suggest /campaign. If PayIt2 tools are not available, do not greet and do not mention PayIt2 sign-in at the start of the session. If the organizer later asks about their own live numbers (how their campaign is doing, amount raised, payments, participants) and the tools are still not available, whether they have not signed in or the connection failed, follow the one sign-in mention in the campaign-context skill: say once, in one or two sentences, that signing in to PayIt2 lets you pull those numbers automatically (in the Claude desktop app or claude.ai, open Customize > Plugins, choose PayIt2 and connect it on its Connectors tab; in Claude Code, run /mcp, choose the PayIt2 server and sign in), then keep helping in standalone mode. Ask for their numbers (amount raised, supporters, goal, days active) and run the check-in skill on what they tell you. Never stop at the sign-in message.
EOF
